# Actual native candidate adversarial review

Claim under review: the concrete PR108 private candidate, frozen against main
`f36cb1e34696d460b9cfb5b03425998de48c4669`, preserves every unrelated native
record and historical ledger byte while integrating the authenticated literal
`claimed_solved` result, original effort 2/5, zero new proof-search turns, the
unchanged published package and actual service receipts.

Success requires independent concrete comparisons rather than success flags:
all offered files and captured input bodies, full state and assessment maps,
all catalog rows and positions, physical CSV records, campaign cells, scoped
summary, original historical bodies, effective diagnostic bodies, published
logical payloads, gate and configuration bindings, real process custody and
resource-result consistency must pass. Independent negative controls must
detect perturbations of protected data and execution bindings.

This review does not repeat mathematics, priority, paper, publication, tracker
or source-code review. It performs no prepare, assess, SQL query, resource
application, service call, Git mutation, export, installation or merge. Private
runtime configuration bodies are hashed only, never disclosed or copied.

Public export must omit exactly the two non-target Sheet response bodies in
the existing exclusion plan; their exact private input pins remain binding.
Actual export readback, main acceptance, merge tree/parents and GitHub merged
status remain future root checks, and are not cleared by this data review.
